## Control {{controlId}}: Terminate User Sessions After Defined Conditions

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization automatically terminates a user session after organization-defined conditions or trigger events within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant. Session termination is enforced through Conditional Access sign-in frequency controls, token lifetime policies, and device configuration idle timeout settings that disconnect inactive or non-compliant sessions.

{{#if conditionalAccessActive}}
Conditional Access policies enforce session termination through {{caPoliciesTotalCount}} configured policies with sign-in frequency controls. Sessions are terminated upon: exceeding the organization-defined inactivity timeout, device compliance status change to non-compliant, user risk level elevation, or token expiration. Re-authentication is required to establish a new session after termination.
{{else}}
Conditional Access session termination policies have not been configured. Session management relies on default Azure AD token lifetime settings pending policy implementation.
{{/if}}

{{#if policies}}
The following policies enforce session termination conditions:
{{#each policies}}
- **{{displayName}}** ({{state}}): Enforces session lifetime controls with {{#each grantControls.builtInControls}}{{this}}{{#unless @last}}, {{/unless}}{{/each}}.
{{/each}}
{{/if}}

{{#if deviceConfigurationsActive}}
Intune device configuration policies ({{deviceConfigurationsCount}} policies) enforce local idle timeout and screen lock settings that complement cloud session termination controls.
{{/if}}

{{#if infraResources}}
Supporting infrastructure:
{{#each infraResources}}
- {{resourceType}} "{{name}}"{{#if properties.retention_days}} (retention: {{properties.retention_days}} days){{/if}}
{{/each}}
{{/if}}

